codex
The failure is caused by the managed sandbox’s PID namespace: processes report an inner PID, while the mounted `/proc` exposes outer PIDs, so Lean’s `IO.appPath` looks up a nonexistent `/proc/<inner-pid>/exe`. I’ve confirmed this independently. I’m applying a narrowly scoped runtime shim under `/tmp/audit-work` that maps `getpid()` to the corresponding visible `NSpid` entry only for the Lean/Lake subprocesses; this does not touch any candidate or provenance file and lets the trusted preflight execute its real clean build.
